  {
   "type": "status",
   "url": "https://x.com/mitchellh/status/2122731286175580550",
   "id": "2122731286175580550",
   "text": "The Rex for Windows alpha begins today! I think this is a better terminal than Windows Terminal, and I think WT is pretty good. Nick did an amazing job here, I think you’re about to feel one of the snappiest, most beautifully rendered Windows apps ever. \n\nThis is all Nicks amazing work but some cool tech details: this is written in Odin! And it’s built on a completely custom GUI framework that leverages native widgets where possible but does plenty of fully custom drawing. The renderer is completely custom and built on DirectX, highly optimized to draw the full UI in one pass and supports things like animation and cursor shaders.\n\nOverall its one hell of a piece of software and I can’t wait for people to feel it.",
   "raw_text": {
    "text": "The Rex for Windows alpha begins today! I think this is a better terminal than Windows Terminal, and I think WT is pretty good. Nick did an amazing job here, I think you’re about to feel one of the snappiest, most beautifully rendered Windows apps ever. \n\nThis is all Nicks amazing work but some cool tech details: this is written in Odin! And it’s built on a completely custom GUI framework that leverages native widgets where possible but does plenty of fully custom drawing. The renderer is completely custom and built on DirectX, highly optimized to draw the full UI in one pass and supports things like animation and cursor shaders.\n\nOverall its one hell of a piece of software and I can’t wait for people to feel it.",
    "display_text_range": [
     0,
     722
    ],
    "facets": []
   },
